<BaseLayout title="UXO.INFO | Unexploded ordnance information" description="A growing public-interest resource on unexploded ordnance, its impacts, and professional clearance.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Field information / public awareness</p><h1>The war ended. The ordnance didn’t.</h1><p class="lead">Unexploded ordnance can remain dangerous long after a conflict has passed. UXO.INFO is building a clearer, source-led way to understand that lasting risk.</p><a class="action-link" href="/what-is-uxo">Start with the basics</a></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2>Knowledge is part of safer ground.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>UXO can affect where people live, farm, rebuild, travel, and recover. Its consequences are not limited to the moment a weapon fails to detonate.</p><p>Our aim is straightforward: make dependable information easier to find, easier to understand, and more useful to people who want to learn, teach, report, or contribute responsibly.</p><a class="action-link" href="/impacts">Explore the impacts</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--deep"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Safety first</p><h2>Information is not clearance.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Suspected explosive ordnance must be left alone and reported to the relevant local authorities or specialist services. UXO.INFO does not provide handling, removal, or disposal instructions.</p><p>Clearance is specialist work: planned, assessed, and carried out by qualified teams under applicable standards and local authority.</p><a class="action-link" href="/clearance">How professional clearance works</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The long view</p><h2>Build carefully. Think beyond one update cycle.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>Maps, regional information, translations, and deeper research tools belong in the next phase—not as empty features now, but as systems we can develop with care and useful source material.</p><p>We also hope that UXO.INFO can one day directly support documented UXO clearance efforts. That is an ambition for the future, not a claim about present funding.</p><p><a href="https://whytrashearth.org" rel="noopener noreferrer">UXO.INFO is a WhyTrashEarth project.</a></p><a class="action-link" href="/vision">The 2045 / 2046 horizon</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
